Widmark's Formula.--The basis for calculating the approximate quantity of alcohol in the body, after equilibrium between the blood and tissues has been reached, is by Widmark's formula:
a = cpr (i) a represents the amount of alcohol expressed in grams;
(ii) c, the amount of alcohol in grams per kg estimated in the blood;
(iii) p is the weight of the person in kg, and (iv) r is the value obtained by dividing the average concentration of alcohol in the body by the concentration of alcohol in the blood.
